# Security baseline invariants

Read `tourism-platform/docs/security/` before auth, token, storage, upload,
AI/RAG, or infrastructure changes. Use Skill `travel-platform-security-audit`
for security-sensitive work.

- All external inputs are untrusted.
- Explicit object/function authorization; UUID is not authZ.
- Parameterized SQL / ORM only; allowlist dynamic identifiers.
- No secrets in Git, images, logs, mobile bundles, or prompts.
- No plaintext/reversible/weak password hashes; Argon2id when auth lands.
- No tokens/passwords in logs, analytics, crash reports, deep links.
- Mobile credentials only via Keychain/Keystore-backed secure storage.
- Explicit request/response DTOs; no ORM dump; no client-set roles/owner.
- No arbitrary HTML, unsafe WebView, or arbitrary server-side URL fetch.
- Enforce limits and timeouts (lists, uploads, providers, AI tools).
- Security-sensitive changes need regression tests.
- Never silently weaken a documented security control.
